<title>NORWAY: Nera sells plant, forms producer alliance.</title>
<headline>Nera sells plant, forms producer alliance.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian telecommunications company Nera ASA said on Wednesday it had signed a letter of intent to sell its plant at Risoer in southern Norway to electronics manufacturer Kitron ASA.</p>
<p>The agreement totals 118 million crowns and part of the transfer settlement will include shares, resulting in Nera gaining a 23.2 percent stake in Kitron, Nera said in a statement.</p>
<p>The companies also agreed to enter a long-term production cooperation agreement, entailing Nera making use of Kitron as a preferred producer of Nera products for a period of 10 years.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
